The discussion revolved around rewordings for a sentence in James's paper on deep uncertainty in the economics literature. The reviewer challenged the original phrasing, suggesting it misleadingly implied consensus among economists regarding approaches to deep uncertainty. In response, several rewordings were proposed, emphasizing the lack of consensus and the varying perspectives on whether deep uncertainty necessitates special treatment. Suggestions included phrasing such as "no consensus on whether deep uncertainty requires treatment beyond conventional decision frameworks" and highlighting competing views among scholars regarding its significance and decision-making implications.
